NNAAMMEE
       pcap‐config  - write libpcap compiler and linker flags to standard out‐
       put

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ppccaapp‐‐ccoonnffiigg [ ----ssttaattiicc ] [ ----ccffllaaggss || ----lliibbss || ----aaddddiittiioonnaall‐‐lliibbss ]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       When run with the ----ccffllaaggss option, _p_c_a_p_‐_c_o_n_f_i_g writes to  the  standard
       output  the  --II  compiler  flags  required  to include libpcap’s header
       files.  When run with the ----lliibbss  option,  _p_c_a_p_‐_c_o_n_f_i_g  writes  to  the
       standard  output the --LL and --ll linker flags required to link with libp‐
       cap, including --ll flags for libraries required by  libpcap.   When  run
       with  the  ----aaddddiittiioonnaall‐‐lliibbss option, _p_c_a_p_‐_c_o_n_f_i_g writes to the standard
       output the --LL and --ll flags for libraries required by libpcap,  but  not
       the --llppccaapp flag to link with libpcap itself.

       By  default,  it  writes flags appropriate for compiling with a dynami‐
       cally‐linked version of libpcap; the ----ssttaattiicc flag causes it  to  write
       flags  appropriate  for  compiling  with a statically‐linked version of
       libpcap.

